        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How the order is worked out",
          "text": "An idea is left to build when it would add something Lion lacks, or when all it needs is something another idea adds. It waits for that other idea when it needs what the other adds, and can start now otherwise. Ideas that can start now are ranked by how much they would give Lion, the features it lacks that they add and the mechanisms they would fold into one, then by how many independent publishers back their techniques. Each run named its features at its own grain, so treat ranks that differ by one as close. An idea passed over is one another idea covers, one that needs something no idea adds, or one that conflicts with what Lion guarantees."
        },
